; CommonTree1 — one of 2 "common" tree picks for the Forest terrain tile
; (terrain.md: emits `forest`; v1's sole harvestable). Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit
; (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; Scale is a FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured fit like the animals (there is no
; "1 tile tall" target for a tree the way there is for a villager). Raw mesh height
; 7.264786 units -> scaled to a target ~2.5-tile canopy height (scale 0.344), a
; stylized-picture-book judgment call, not derived from any GDD number. FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF: this is exactly the kind of look-affecting parameter the tech-art boundary
; reserves for the human's eyeball call.
;
; SLAB REINSTATED (2026-08-03): TerrainView._refresh_tile_visual() instantiates
; model_scene as a tile's ENTIRE visual — nothing else is drawn per tile — and this prop
; alone (trunk + canopy) doesn't cover the tile's footprint. Without a slab, the rest of
; the tile showed scenes/Main.tscn's configured WorldEnvironment sky-blue background_color
; (0.53, 0.72, 0.86) showing straight through the gap, which an in-engine human look
; reported as "a lot of transparency, lots of blue showing." This was confirmed by that
; look, not assumed. Slab geometry/position/color are
; copied verbatim from the grey-box placeholder this scene replaced
; (assets/placeholder/forest/Forest.tscn) — same taste call, not a new one. The look of
; the prop-on-slab combo still awaits full human sign-off.
;
; FLOOR BLOTCH PATCHES ADDED (2026-08-16): human complaint — "floor should not just be a
; solid color." No tileable ground texture exists in the already-audited MegaKit files
; (Grass.png etc. are thin UV-strip palette textures for vertex-style mesh coloring, not
; tiling ground textures — confirmed by inspection, not assumed), so per the task's
; explicit fallback this uses a BLOTCHY MULTI-TONE color treatment instead of a shader
; rewrite: 3 flat, unlit-color PlaneMesh patches (moss-dark-green and leaf-litter-brown)
; laid 0.001 units above the slab top to avoid z-fighting, at varied position/rotation —
; same "small mesh, varied placement" idiom as the grass/rock scatter passes, applied to
; color instead of props. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: whether 3 patches read as "mottled
; forest floor" rather than as stray shapes, and the exact tones chosen.
;
; ALL GROUND MESHES NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (2026-08-16, required, not
; cosmetic): OcclusionFader._collect_fadeable_meshes() (scripts/world/occlusion_fader.gd)
; skips exactly one node by exact name match, "Slab", and returns without recursing into
; it — the mechanism that keeps the ground plane from ever being faded ("fading it would
; open a transparent hole in the ground, not 'see past the tree'", its own header). The 3
; floor patches are ground decals, not tree parts, so they need the same exemption; as
; flat siblings of "Slab" they were NOT exempt and OcclusionFader picked them up as
; fadeable tree material by mistake (caught by test_occlusion_fader.gd's precondition
; checks). Fixed by moving the BoxMesh ground plane (renamed "Ground") and all 3 patches
; to be CHILDREN of one wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab", at identity transform so
; every child keeps its previous absolute-equivalent transform unchanged.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported): human eyeball pass on the prior
; look-pass reported "tiles did not have separation between each tile, so you can't tell
; where the first tile ends and the next tile begins" — the OPPOSITE of the intended read.
; `WorldGrid.TILE_SIZE` is 1.0 (world_grid.gd), so a 0.94 slab left a real 0.03-unit gap on
; every tile edge showing the sky-blue WorldEnvironment background straight through between
; adjacent tiles. Widened X/Z to exactly 1.0 (an exact `TILE_SIZE` match, not a tiny
; overlap — 1.0 is exactly representable in float, so adjacent tile edges meet with no
; accumulation error) so neighboring slabs' edges touch with no gap. Y (height, 0.2)
; untouched. Applied identically across all 10 composed terrain scenes this pass touches —
; see content-pipeline-status.md -> Terrain for the full list.
[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

